/**
 * Applies a JSON Merge Patch to a task, every property edited in place: a member left out is
 * unchanged, `null` clears what can be empty.
 *
 * - `status`: any status, from any other, but one the space no longer uses
 *   (`422 task.status-hidden`, unless the task already has it). `cancelled` needs
 *   `cancelReason` (`422 task.cancel-reason-required`) and takes `cancelNote`; on a cancelled
 *   task, they change alone; on a task that is not cancelled after the patch they answer
 *   `422 task.cancel-reason-unexpected`. Leaving `cancelled` clears them, entering `done` sets
 *   `completedAt` and leaving it clears it.
 * - `dueDate`: when the task has a start date, a new due date moves the start by as many
 *   days and keeps the duration, unless the patch sets `startDate` too; removing the due date
 *   removes the start. `startDate` needs a due date and is on or before it
 *   (`422 task.start-date-invalid`).
 * - `listId` ("Déplacer vers…", "CAD-482 déplacée", "Vers Bugs."): the task moves to the list,
 *   in this space or another, with its subtasks, and keeps its key; a subtask leaves its
 *   parent first. A list the caller does not see answers `422 task.list-invalid`.
 * - `parentKey` ("Devenir sous-tâche de…", "CAD-490 rattachée à CAD-482"): the task becomes a
 *   subtask of a task the caller sees, and moves with its subtasks to the list of the parent.
 *   The parent may be neither the task nor one of its subtasks, nor unknown
 *   (`422 task.parent-invalid`); the task and its subtasks must fit within 3 levels under it
 *   (`422 task.subtask-depth-exceeded`), and the parent must have fewer than 25 subtasks
 *   (`422 task.subtask-limit-reached`). With `listId` in the same patch, it must be the list
 *   of the parent (`422 task.list-invalid`). `null` detaches it ("CAD-490 détachée", "C’est
 *   de nouveau une tâche de premier niveau."); it stays in its list.
 * - The statuses a space no longer uses are those of the space the task is in after the
 *   patch: a move or an attachment keeps the status the task has, even one the new space no
 *   longer uses, while a new `status` in the same patch must be used by the new space.
 * - `customFieldValues`: set or clear values by active definition ID. A move to another
 *   space removes incompatible values from the moved tasks in the same transaction. IDs in
 *   this patch must belong to the resulting space and values must match their definitions
 *   (`422 custom-field.value-invalid`). A null entry clears that value. Other entries remain
 *   unchanged for a task that stays in its space. No custom values are copied to a successor.
 * - `If-Match` is optional (`412 request.version-mismatch`), but required to change
 *   `description`, a long text: without it, `400 request.invalid` with an issue on the
 *   header.
 * - `If-Organization-Match` optionally pins the change to the caller's expected organization.
 *   The gateway checks it before forwarding the change. `If-Match` still checks the task
 *   version within the verified organization.
 * - It needs `edit` on the list of the task, and on the list it moves to
 *   (`403 access.role-insufficient`). An archived task answers `409 task.archived`, and so
 *   does an archived parent, `details.key` naming the archived task.
 *
 * Records the changes of status, priority and due date in the activity log. Emits
 * `task.updated.v1` when something changed, with `changed`, and also
 * `task.status-changed.v1` for a new status; a move emits `task.updated.v1` for each subtask
 * that moves too. An updated task's event can name `customFieldValues` in `changed`;
 * the event never carries the custom values themselves.
 * A patch that changes nothing answers `200` with the same version and emits
 * nothing. Scope `tasks:write` for a personal API token.
 * Description mentions require If-Match, including spans-only changes. Replacing text clears
 * old spans unless replacements are supplied. Milestone conversion and recurrence follow
 * the shared TaskPatch rules. Entering done with a due date creates at most one root successor
 * in the same list, atomically with resetting recurrence to none, the link and the outbox.
 * Cancellation, an undated completion, a repeated done, creation in done and restore create
 * none. A source that has already spawned cannot be rearmed (`409 recurrence.already-spawned`).
 * Unrepresentable dates answer `422 recurrence.date-out-of-range`. A successor copies the
 * title, Markdown, priority, labels, eligible assignees, ordinary estimate, milestone and
 * unchecked checklist, with a fresh key and todo status. It excludes children, parent,
 * mentions, comments, watcher overrides, dependencies and completion metadata. Start dates
 * move by the due-date delta and milestones retain date alignment. Monthly cadence retains
 * the original day across short months. Fresh watcher defaults apply. A live existing task
 * entering done as a milestone emits milestone.reached.v1, including when the same patch
 * adds the flag. Creation in done, restore, cancellation, repeated done and adding the flag
 * to an already-done task do not; a later genuine transition into done can emit it again.
 * @summary Change a task
 */
export const updateTaskPathTaskKeyRegExp = new RegExp('^[A-Z]{2,5}-[1-9][0-9]{0,8}$');


export const UpdateTaskParams = zod.object({
  "taskKey": zod.string().regex(updateTaskPathTaskKeyRegExp).describe('Key of the task.')
})

export const updateTaskHeaderIfOrganizationMatchRegExp = new RegExp('^[0-9A-Fa-f]{8}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{4}-7[0-9A-Fa-f]{3}-[89ABab][0-9A-Fa-f]{3}-[0-9A-Fa-f]{12}$');


export const UpdateTaskHeader = zod.object({
  "If-Match": zod.string().optional().describe('`"<version>"` of the task the change was made from, as the `ETag` gave it.'),
  "If-Organization-Match": zod.uuid().regex(updateTaskHeaderIfOrganizationMatchRegExp).optional().describe('The UUIDv7 of the organization the caller expects, compared without regard to hex case.\nThe verified session or API token determines the organization for the request. The gateway\nuses this header only to check that organization before forwarding the request. A mismatch\nanswers `412 organization.context-changed`. Omit the header to use the verified context\nwithout an organization precondition. Send exactly one UUIDv7: repeated, comma-separated\nor malformed values answer `400 request.invalid` with an issue on this header.\n')
})

